The severe weather conditions have led to the devastation of over 20,000 residences, displacing 122,000 individuals who now reside in government-operated temporary shelters. Over 833,000 individuals needed aid after being uprooted by the floods. Personnel from the army, navy, and air force have been dispatched to assist in the relief efforts. Access to the internet has also faced interruptions.

