In Victoria, the municipality has added 30 more shelter mats, with overnight accommodations available at 525 Johnson St. beginning at 8 p.m. on Friday and concluding at 7 a.m. on Saturday. Additionally, daytime public warming facilities are available at various locations, including Saanich Commonwealth Place, Gordon Head Recreation Centre, Cedar Hill Recreation and Arts Centre, and G.R. Pearkes Recreation Centre. Operational hours for these facilities may fluctuate due to severe weather conditions and staffing availability.

Both EWR beds and regular nightly shelter accommodations are distinct, with EWR beds specifically deployed when a warning of severe weather conditions arises. The forecast predicts winds up to 30 kilometers per hour with gusts reaching 70 kilometers per hour near the Juan de Fuca Strait, before easing overnight.
