The city stated that their extreme-weather protocol ensures community members can find refuge in a secure, heated shelter when the weather turns bitterly cold. Individuals seeking overnight accommodation are advised to visit Potter's House at Jefferson Elementary, located at 612 S. College Avenue, by 5 p.m. Meals for both dinner and breakfast will be included.

Activation is currently limited to Saturday, Jan. 17, although the Fayetteville C.R.E.W. team remains vigilant, assessing weather conditions daily. For further inquiries, the city's Cold Weather Hotline is available at 479-259-2428.
