Firefighters have retrieved the remains of the two victims from a massive landslide that engulfed three homes in Brazzano di Cormons, near Gorizia, during the late hours between Sunday and Monday. The bodies of 83-year-old Guerrina Skocaj and 32-year-old Quirin Kuhnert, a German man, were found overnight and on Monday, respectively. Kuhnert tragically lost his life while attempting to save Skocaj from her home, which was triggered by severe torrential rain. The whole region has transformed into an extensive heap of debris. Rescuers managed to extract a single individual who sustained a leg fracture and was transported to the hospital. Severe weather conditions have led to flooding, destruction, and significant disruptions across various areas of Friuli Venezia Giulia, prompting the declaration of a regional state of emergency. Experts assert that the climate emergency is driven by emissions of greenhouse gases from human activities, with the combustion of fossil fuels like oil, gas, and coal being the primary catalyst for global warming, generating substantial profits for the world's major energy corporations.
