Class 4 impact-resistant shingles, designed to withstand the impact of large hailstones and severe weather conditions, have become the exclusive choice for Calgary-based No Payne Roofing. "At No Payne, our installations feature only Class 4 shingles due to their hail-resistant and hail-proof qualities, ensuring long-lasting durability and minimizing home damage," said Mike Payne, owner of No Payne Roofing. "Though Class 4 shingles might eventually become a building code standard, they currently offer an excellent way to save time, money, and the inconvenience of insurance claims."

Despite the robust protection provided by Class 4 shingles, the condition of the underlying structure remains crucial. Plywood typically lasts around 50 years under optimal conditions, but exposure to severe weather can shorten this lifespan. Payne emphasizes that replacing old plywood during re-roofing is a critical yet frequently neglected task. His Calgary team guarantees that the plywood they install will match the lifespan of the new shingles.

Many older homes in Calgary feature plywood roof decking installed over four decades ago. Laying new roofing on aging plywood can cause performance problems and potentially nullify manufacturer warranties, as roofing material producers often specify specific age and quality standards for the underlying structure. Payne’s team ensures that worn-out plywood is replaced during re-roofing to maintain the integrity of the entire roofing system.
