Similar to other Mediterranean nations, Türkiye has been experiencing an increase in extreme weather incidents over recent years as the repercussions of climate change accelerate, posing significant threats to rural agricultural communities. Mehmet Akın Doğan, the president of the Yüreğir Chamber of Agriculture, noted that farmers in the productive Çukurova Valley near Adana, responsible for nearly 40 percent of Türkiye's citrus yield, are facing escalating challenges.

