Jamaica, as an island nation, faced significant challenges in the wake of Hurricane Melissa, resulting in obstacles to both relief initiatives and damage evaluation processes. Jamaican Prime Minister Andrew Holness (@andrewholnessjm) posted a segment of his conversation with CNN anchor Anderson Cooper, coupled with a message directed at his constituents. "Your homes might have suffered damage or been completely destroyed, and your communities and towns now appear different. I understand your suffering and share in your grief," Holness wrote.

